    "body": "I'm waiting on the FPWD for the relevant [CSS spec](https://github.com/w3c/transitions/issues/461) before this can land. But wanted to get an early review on the spec change.\r\n\r\nThis is related to the CSSWG issue [here](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/7784). The high level context is that for cross-document [view transitions](https://github.com/WICG/shared-element-transitions/blob/main/explainer.md), we can use the existing concept of [render-blocking](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#render-blocked) to delay the start of the transition until the new Document is ready. But for same-document transitions the same behaviour (pausing rendering opportunities) needs to be explicitly defined.\r\n\r\nOne aspect I was unsure about is that suppressing rendering on a Document implies visual updates from nested Documents will also not be drawn. I'm not sure if this needs to be explicitly specified or if that's implied. Happy to file an issue if this needs more discussion.",
